{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.SheafHom","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Subsheaf"],"declarations":61,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorSiteGerbe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorSiteGerbe","kind":"def","line":565,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L565-L580","doc":"**Instantiation of `SiteGerbeData J A` by the torsor gerbe `Tors(A)` (Milestone 3).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.bandEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.bandEquiv","kind":"def","line":562,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L562-L562","doc":"(4) Band isomorphism on the neutral object over every `X : C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.locallyConnected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.locallyConnected","kind":"theorem","line":559,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L559-L559","doc":"(3) Local connectedness: any two objects are locally isomorphic on a `J`-covering sieve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.hom_isIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.hom_isIso","kind":"theorem","line":556,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L556-L556","doc":"(2) Groupoid fibres: every `A`-equivariant morphism between objects is an isomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.hom_isSheaf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.hom_isSheaf","kind":"theorem","line":553,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L553-L553","doc":"(1) Descent of morphisms: `equivariantHom` between any two objects is a `J`-sheaf. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.neutral","kind":"def","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L551-L551","doc":"Distinguished neutral object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.actionOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.actionOf","kind":"def","line":549,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L549-L549","doc":"Underlying `A`-action of an object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.presheafOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.presheafOf","kind":"def","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L547-L547","doc":"Underlying presheaf of an object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.Obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.Obj","kind":"def","line":545,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L545-L545","doc":"Type of objects of the gerbe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":543,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L543-L543","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SiteGerbeData","kind":"structure","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L531-L563","doc":"Genuine Grothendieck-topology **gerbe data** (`SiteGerbeData J A`) banded by a\nsheaf of groups `A` on a site `(C, J)`, capturing the four defining properties of\n`Tors(A)`:\n1. **Descent of morphisms (prestack axiom):** for any objects `T₁, T₂`, the presheaf of\n   morphisms between `T₁` and `T₂` is a `J`-sheaf.\n2. **Groupoid fibres (`Hom = Iso`):** every morphism between objects over `C/X` is an\n   isomorphism.\n3. **Non-emptiness:** the category of objects is inhabited (hence locally non-empty).\n4. **Local connectedness:** for any two objects `T₁, T₂` and any `U : C`, the sieve of\n   morphisms `V ⟶ U` over which `T₁` and `T₂` become isomorphic belongs to `J U`.\n5. **Band isomorphism:** the endomorphisms of the distinguished object over `X` are in\n   bijection with `A.obj (op X)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorPullback_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorPullback_comp","kind":"theorem","line":522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L522-L529","doc":"Base-change along a composite `f ≫ g` equals the composite of the base-change functors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorPullback_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorPullback_id","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L513-L520","doc":"Base-change along the identity morphism `𝟙 X` is the identity functor on `TorsorFibre J A X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorPullback","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorPullback","kind":"def","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L503-L511","doc":"Base-change functor `TorsorFibre J A Y ⥤ TorsorFibre J A X` along a morphism\n`f : X ⟶ Y` in `C`, restricting `A`-equivariant morphisms along `Over.map f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorFibreGroupoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorFibreGroupoid","kind":"instance","line":488,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L488-L501","doc":"**Groupoid instance on `TorsorFibre J A X` (Milestone 2/3):** every `A`-equivariant\nmorphism between `A`-torsors over `C/X` is an isomorphism (`isIso_of_equivariantHom_torsor`)\nwith `A`-equivariant inverse (`inv_mem_equivariantHom`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorFibreCategory","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsorFibreCategory","kind":"instance","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L478-L486","doc":"Category instance on `TorsorFibre J A X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.TorsorFibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.TorsorFibre","kind":"def","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L470-L476","doc":"The fibre category `TorsorFibre J A X` of `A`-torsors over `X : C`, whose objects are\nmultiplicative `A`-torsors and whose morphisms `T₁ ⟶ T₂` are `A`-equivariant morphisms\n`T₁.carrier|_{C/X} ⟶ T₂.carrier|_{C/X}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor.isMulAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor.isMulAction","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L468-L468","doc":"Compatibility of the action with the group structure on `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor.torsor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor.torsor","kind":"def","line":466,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L466-L466","doc":"Torsor structure on `carrier`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor.carrier","kind":"def","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L464-L464","doc":"Underlying presheaf of the torsor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L461-L461","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.MulSheafTorsor","kind":"structure","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L459-L468","doc":"A multiplicative `A`-torsor on `(C, J)`, bundling `SheafTorsor J A P` with\n`action.IsMulAction`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsor_locallyConnected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.torsor_locallyConnected","kind":"theorem","line":444,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L444-L457","doc":"**Local connectedness of `Tors(A)` (Milestone 3).** For any two multiplicative\n`A`-torsors `TP` and `TQ` on `(C, J)` and any `U : C`, the sieve `localIsoSieve` of\nmorphisms `f : V ⟶ U` over which `P|_{C/V}` and `Q|_{C/V}` are `A`-equivariantly\nisomorphic belongs to `J U`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.localIsoSieve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.localIsoSieve","kind":"def","line":432,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L432-L442","doc":"The sieve of morphisms `f : V ⟶ U` over which two `A`-presheaves `(P, αP)` and\n`(Q, αQ)` admit an `A`-equivariant isomorphism `P|_{C/V} ≅ Q|_{C/V}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom_of_sections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom_of_sections","kind":"def","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L384-L430","doc":"Given two multiplicative pseudo-torsors `(P, αP)` and `(Q, αQ)` and sections\n`p₀ ∈ P(V)` and `q₀ ∈ Q(V)`, there is a canonical `A`-equivariant morphism\n`P|_{C/V} ⟶ Q|_{C/V}` sending the restrictions of `p₀` to the restrictions of `q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.trivialTorsorEndEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.trivialTorsorEndEquiv","kind":"def","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L336-L382","doc":"**Band isomorphism for the trivial `A`-torsor (`Aut(trivial) ≃ A(X)`).**\nFor any presheaf of groups `A` and any object `X : C`, the `A`-equivariant endomorphisms\nof the trivial `A`-torsor over `C/X` are in canonical bijection with `A.obj (op X)` via\nevaluation at `1 ∈ A.obj (op X)` at `Over.mk (𝟙 X)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.trivialSheafTorsor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.trivialSheafTorsor","kind":"def","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L327-L334","doc":"The **trivial `A`-torsor** on `(C, J)` associated to a `J`-sheaf of groups `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.locallyNonempty_of_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.locallyNonempty_of_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L315-L325","doc":"Any presheaf with a global section over every `U` is locally non-empty for every\nGrothendieck topology `J`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.isPseudoTorsor_regularAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.isPseudoTorsor_regularAction","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L307-L313","doc":"The regular action of a presheaf of groups `A` on itself is a pseudo-torsor:\nfor any `p, q ∈ A(U)`, `a = q * p⁻¹` is the unique element satisfying `a * p = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.isMulAction_regularAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.isMulAction_regularAction","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L301-L305","doc":"The regular action of `A` on itself is a multiplicative action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.regularAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.regularAction","kind":"def","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L295-L299","doc":"The regular left action of a presheaf of groups `A` on itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsMulAction.mul_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsMulAction.mul_smul","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L292-L292","doc":"Product acts by iterated action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsMulAction.one_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsMulAction.one_smul","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L290-L290","doc":"Identity element acts trivially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsMulAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsMulAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L287-L287","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsMulAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsMulAction","kind":"structure","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L286-L293","doc":"Compatibility of a `PresheafAction A P` with the sectionwise group multiplication on `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.IsPresheafOfGroups.map_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.IsPresheafOfGroups.map_one","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L284-L284","doc":"Restriction preserves the identity element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.IsPresheafOfGroups.map_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.IsPresheafOfGroups.map_mul","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L282-L282","doc":"Restriction preserves multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.IsPresheafOfGroups.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.IsPresheafOfGroups.mk","kind":"ctor","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L280-L280","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.IsPresheafOfGroups","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.IsPresheafOfGroups","kind":"structure","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L278-L284","doc":"Compatibility of a presheaf `A` carrying sectionwise group structure `[∀ U, Group (A.obj U)]`\nwith restriction maps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.inv_mem_equivariantHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.inv_mem_equivariantHom","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L254-L274","doc":"The inverse of an `A`-equivariant isomorphism of `A`-presheaves is again\n`A`-equivariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.comp_mem_equivariantHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.comp_mem_equivariantHom","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L238-L252","doc":"The composition of two `A`-equivariant morphisms over `C/X` is `A`-equivariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.id_mem_equivariantHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.id_mem_equivariantHom","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L233-L236","doc":"The identity morphism of `P|_{C/X}` is `A`-equivariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.isIso_of_equivariantHom_torsor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.isIso_of_equivariantHom_torsor","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L220-L231","doc":"**`Hom = Iso` on `A`-torsors (Milestone 2).** Every `A`-equivariant morphism\n`φ : P|_{C/X} ⟶ Q|_{C/X}` between `A`-torsors on `(C, J)` is an isomorphism of\npresheaves on `(Over X.unop)ᵒᵖ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L167-L218","doc":"Every `A`-equivariant morphism between `A`-torsors is sectionwise surjective: local\npreimages on the `J`-covering sieve where `P` is non-empty agree on overlaps by\n`equivariantHom_injective`, hence glue in the sheaf `P` to a global preimage. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom_surjective_of_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom_surjective_of_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L152-L165","doc":"At any object `Y` where `P` has a section, every `A`-equivariant morphism into a\npseudo-torsor `Q` is surjective on sections over `Y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom_injective","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L130-L150","doc":"Every `A`-equivariant morphism between pseudo-torsors is sectionwise injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.locallyNonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.locallyNonempty","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L128-L128","doc":"`P` has local sections on a `J`-covering sieve of every object `U`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.isPseudoTorsor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.isPseudoTorsor","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L126-L126","doc":"The action of `A` on sections of `P` is simply transitive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.isSheaf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.isSheaf","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L124-L124","doc":"`P` is a `J`-sheaf. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.action","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L122-L122","doc":"The underlying `A`-action on `P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L120-L120","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.SheafTorsor","kind":"structure","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L118-L128","doc":"An **`A`-torsor** (`SheafTorsor J A P`) on a site `(C, J)` is a `J`-sheaf `P`\nequipped with a pseudo-torsor action of `A` that is locally non-empty with respect to `J`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.LocallyNonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.LocallyNonempty","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L113-L116","doc":"A presheaf `P` is **locally non-empty** with respect to a Grothendieck topology `J`\nif for every object `U : C`, `localNonemptySieve P U` belongs to `J U`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.localNonemptySieve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.localNonemptySieve","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L108-L111","doc":"The sieve of morphisms `f : V ⟶ U` over which `P(V)` is non-empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsPseudoTorsor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.IsPseudoTorsor","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L102-L106","doc":"A presheaf action `αP` of `A` on `P` is a **pseudo-torsor** (formal principal\nhomogeneous space) if for every `U` and every pair of sections `p, q ∈ P(U)`, there is a\nunique operator `a ∈ A(U)` sending `p` to `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.isSheaf_equivariantHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.isSheaf_equivariantHom","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L72-L98","doc":"**Descent of morphisms for `A`-presheaves.** If `Q` is a sheaf, the presheaf of\n`A`-equivariant morphisms `P|_{C/X} ⟶ Q|_{C/X}` is a sheaf, for every presheaf `P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.equivariantHom","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L64-L70","doc":"The subpresheaf of `presheafHom P Q` of `A`-equivariant morphisms over `C/X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.map_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.map_smul","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Restriction commutes with the action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.smul","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The action on sections over `U`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StackGerbe.PresheafAction","kind":"structure","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StackGerbe.lean#L52-L60","doc":"An action of a presheaf of operators `A` on a presheaf `P`, natural in the base.\nFor a presheaf of groups `G` take `A = G ⋙ forget GrpCat`. The group axioms are not\nneeded for the descent-of-morphisms statement below, so they are not imposed here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}